                                  "data-styles-preset": `vJYEnMnRI`,
                                  dir: `auto`,
                                  style: { "--framer-text-alignment": `justify` },
                                  children: `The core concept of the game is following the story of the protagonist through occasional diary entries which ties in with some major events in the protagonist's life. There are also some minor details in some stages that imply some sort of optional choices that can affect how the story is perceived, such as putting an item into the bag over another. In some cases, the rules were written in a non-specific way where it doesn't explicitly state what items to bring, but rather what kind of it. Technically speaking, this is designed by creating tags for each items, and each rule in a stage requires a certain tag of items or a specific item. This gives players some restricted freedom on what they want to bring and what stays behind. The illusion of freedom, if you will, is designed to create an active participation and a form of immersion into the story, making the players have a sense of responsibility to the protagonist's story.`,
