                                  className: `framer-styles-preset-17ydyq9`,
                                  "data-styles-preset": `vJYEnMnRI`,
                                  dir: `auto`,
                                  style: { "--framer-text-alignment": `justify` },
                                  children: `Other than the gameplay, the presence of multiple items in the game opens up plenty of room for visual storytelling.. On the other hand, the fact that items need to fit in with the story means that there are issues with how much visual assets we needed to make for the game. Because of it, I needed to design the levels and write the story in a way that it balances new items and reoccurring items. I made some items to be what the protagonist consider as precious, making it reappear in future stages.  Other than that, there are also items that are simply recolors of previous ones, such as socks. This naturally reduces the need to make unique assets for stages. Of course, we didn't do this much since we still wanted to create items that have specific meaning in certain points of the story.`,
